    "judge_reasoning": "Dataset is small (1800 train) with 150x150 single-channel images; both under/overfitting observed, so aim for mid-sized capacity with good optimization. Likely sweet spot is ~1\u20135M params; <0.1M risks underfitting; >10M likely overfits without heavy regularization/augmentation. ResNet skip connections generally make deeper models easier to optimize at given capacity, so prefer moderate-depth ResNets over similarly sized plain CNNs, but extremely deep/huge models are too much. Top picks: [4] 1.23M ResNet wide-shallow should fit without severe overfit and train stably; [2] 2.8M ResNet small provides more representational power while still plausible for 1.8k samples; [3]/[6] 1.9\u20132.5M CNNs are similar capacity but may be a bit harder to optimize/generalize than ResNets. Midplus ResNet [7] at 4.7M may work but higher overfit risk. Wide CNN [8] similar params but very wide late layers could overfit. Deep-narrow ResNet [5] 3.34M but deeper (16 blocks) may be ok though could over-regularize/overfit depending; placed mid. Tiny models [0],[1] likely underfit. Very large ResNet [9] 31M is least promising due to strong overfitting risk on 1.8k samples.",
